{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואכלו את הבשר", :translit "v'achalu et ha-basar", :gloss "and they shall eat the flesh"} {:he "על מרורים יאכלוהו", :translit "al m'rorim y'och'luhu", :gloss "on bitter herbs they shall eat it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse begins and ends with root אכל, hinting two separate obligatory eatings"}], :frame {:text "The flesh of the Paschal lamb must be eaten when one is satisfied from the festival offering (chagigah), so that the Pesach is eaten \"when sated\" (פסח נאכל על השובע). This requirement is derived from the words אותו in Deuteronomy 16:2, which teaches that the Pesach is eaten upon another offering. The underlying rule is that the Paschal lamb is eaten by a group at the conclusion of the meal (Pesach 70a; Mishnah Pesachim 10:3–4).", :sources ["Deuteronomy 16:2" "Mishnah Pesachim 10:3" "Pesachim 70a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יאכלהו", :translit "y'och'luhu", :gloss "they shall eat it"} {:he "אל תאכלו", :translit "al tochlü", :gloss "you shall not eat"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contextual adjacency of the adjacent verse forbidding leftover consumption teaches the eating must be with intent for the mitzvah"}], :frame {:text "The adjacent prohibition is Exodus 12:10 — ולא תותירו ממנו עד בקר ואת הנותר ממנו באש תשרפו — referring to not leaving over and burning the remainder. The Pesach must be eaten לשמה, with intent for the mitzvah, which entails eating from a position of hunger rather than pure gluttony. The concept of intent (kavvanah) for the Paschal offering is addressed in Pesachim 61a.", :sources ["Exodus 12:10" "Pesachim 61a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יאכלוהו", :translit "y'och'luhu", :gloss "they shall eat it"} {:he "אהרן ובניו יאכלוהו", :translit "Aharon u-vanav y'och'luhu", :gloss "Aaron and his sons shall eat it"} {:he "ומפתח אוהל מועד לא תצאו", :translit "u-mi-petach ohel mo'ed lo tze'u", :gloss "and from the entrance of the Tent of Meeting you shall not go out"} {:he "ואתם לא תצאו איש מפתח ביתו", :translit "v'atem lo tze'u ish mi-petach beito", :gloss "and you shall not go out, a man from the door of his house"} {:he "כי מאספיו יאכלוהו", :translit "ki m'as'pav y'och'luhu", :gloss "those gathered for it shall eat it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ואכלו את הבשר ... על מרורים יאכלוהו" "ואכלהו ... אל תאכלו" "אהרן ובניו יאכלוהו" "כי מאספיו יאכלוהו"]}], :frame {:text "The ordination installation of Aaron and his sons lasted seven days, during which they ate the ordination ram and were forbidden to leave the Tent of Meeting (Exodus 29:31–33; Leviticus 8:31–35). The Passover night similarly forbids leaving the house (Exodus 12:22). The verse כי מאספיו יאכלוהו in Isaiah 65:8 — literally referring to those assembled — is read as a future eschatological meal, linking the exodus to the messianic redemption. This typological link between the Egyptian exodus and the final redemption is prophesied in Jeremiah 16:14–15, where God swears by \"who brought Israel up from the land of the north,\" equating the future ingathering with the first exodus.", :sources ["Exodus 29:31-33" "Leviticus 8:31-35" "Exodus 12:22" "Isaiah 65:8" "Jeremiah 16:14-15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse begins and ends with root אכל, hinting two separate obligatory eatings", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Contextual adjacency of the adjacent verse forbidding leftover consumption teaches the eating must be with intent for the mitzvah", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ואכלו את הבשר ... על מרורים יאכלוהו" "ואכלהו ... אל תאכלו" "אהרן ובניו יאכלוהו" "כי מאספיו יאכלוהו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ואכלו את הבשר ... על מרורים יאכלוהו", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ואכלהו ... אל תאכלו", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "אהרן ובניו יאכלוהו", :refs ["Leviticus 8:31"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "כי מאספיו יאכלוהו", :refs ["Isaiah 62:9"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:19.421214550Z", :model "glm-5.2"}